  "id": "Compound::DB00204 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Dofetilide is implicated in the regulation of Cyp3a4 through a series of molecular interactions involving the paralytic effect of its metabolites. The evidence suggests that Dofetilide causes Paralysis Flaccid, which is then mediated by different compounds—Methazolamide, Acetazolamide, and Histamine Phosphate—all of which bind to Cyp3a4. These compounds are all classified as organic cyclic compounds or pnictogen molecular entities, indicating a common structural motif. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Dofetilide indirectly influences Cyp3a4, likely through the metabolic activation of its metabolites. The recurring role of organic cyclic compounds and the shared causal pathway from Dofetilide to Paralysis Flaccid suggest a consistent molecular mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
